      "id": "a4615d3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Background of Economic Reforms"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Economic Reforms were launched in 1991 under PM P. V. Narasimha Rao and Finance Minister Dr. Manmohan Singh to tackle a severe Balance of Payments crisis.",
        "Liberalization aimed at ending the 'Licensing Raj', reducing import tariffs, and deregulating industrial sectors.",
        "Privatization focused on disinvesting government stake in Public Sector Undertakings (PSUs) and enhancing private participation.",
        "Globalization aimed to integrate the Indian economy with the world market through FDI promotion and replacing FERA with FEMA."
      ],
      "id": "2rctfdp"
