    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "The 1991 economic reform policy is commonly referred to as the Rao-Manmohan Model of development.",
        "FERA (Foreign Exchange Regulation Act, 1973) was replaced by FEMA (Foreign Exchange Management Act, 1999) to liberalize foreign trade.",
        "High inflation, depletion of foreign exchange reserves to less than two weeks of imports, and fiscal deficit were the primary triggers for the reforms."
      ],
      "id": "pewkcl4"
